stimulus.description:
A parking garage is writing a class ParkingFee with two static methods that compute the charge for a stay measured in whole minutes.
```java
public class ParkingFee {
    /** Returns the number of hours charged for a stay of the given number of minutes.
     *  Any fraction of an hour counts as a full hour, and 0 minutes is 0 hours. Precondition: minutes >= 0. */
    public static int hoursCharged(int minutes) { /* part (a) */ }

    /** Returns the total fee, in dollars, for a stay of the given number of minutes.
     *  The first two charged hours cost 4 dollars each, every additional charged hour costs 3 dollars,
     *  and the total never exceeds 20 dollars. Precondition: minutes >= 0. */
    public static int totalFee(int minutes) { /* part (b) */ }
}
```

parts.model_answer:
One correct implementation (ALTON reference answer):
```java
    public static int hoursCharged(int minutes) {
        int hours = minutes / 60;
        if (minutes % 60 != 0) {
            hours++;
        }
        return hours;
    }
```

One correct implementation (ALTON reference answer):
```java
    public static int totalFee(int minutes) {
        int h = hoursCharged(minutes);
        int fee;
        if (h <= 2) {
            fee = 4 * h;
        } else {
            fee = 8 + 3 * (h - 2);
        }
        if (fee > 20) {
            fee = 20;
        }
        return fee;
    }
```

